---
source: crates/trust-cg-test/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help_of(&[\"ratchet\", \"panic-clippy\"])"
---
Baseline-aware clippy gate for production panic-family diagnostics.

Runs `scripts/check_panic_clippy.sh` through the `trust-cg-test` ratchet dispatcher, preserving the
script's workspace package discovery, `--package` filtering, deny-level panic-family clippy lints,
and `ratchet/unwrap_baseline.json` comparison behavior. Full runs also execute the unwrap regex
ratchet unless `--skip-ratchet` is set.

Exit codes match the underlying script:
  0 — panic-family diagnostics are within baseline.
  1 — production panic-family diagnostics exceed baseline.
  2 — tooling error, missing baseline, or invalid args.

# Examples

  trust-cg-test ratchet panic-clippy
  trust-cg-test ratchet panic-clippy --package trust-cg-test
  trust-cg-test ratchet panic-clippy --package trust-cg-test --skip-ratchet

Usage: trust-cg-test ratchet panic-clippy [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format (human, json, junit)

          Possible values:
          - human: Pretty table + narrative, targeted at humans
          - json:  Machine-readable JSON
          - junit: JUnit XML for CI consumers

          [default: human]

  -p, --package <NAME>
          Check only one workspace package. May be repeated

  -o, --out <PATH>
          Override the command-specific output file or directory.

          See the selected subcommand's help for its output type and default.

      --skip-ratchet
          Skip the full unwrap ratchet; intended for focused local clippy probes

      --timeout <SECS>
          Per-unit timeout in seconds. Subcommands may apply per-unit defaults when this is unset

      --parallel <N>
          Worker count (honors cargo-serialization lock). Default: auto

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress progress bars; errors still go to stderr

  -v, --verbose...
          Show debug-level events. Repeat for more: -vv, -vvv

      --no-cache
          Ignore proof / corpus caches

      --dry-run
          Print what would run without executing external tools

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
